              "payload": "tree 9e3f02fdf0d5ca39f41fd0a69307b0eeedd5d53d\nparent 409b8f9312ae9e2e0b4a0ae086f64d1fa2abc6bb\nauthor paseo-bot[bot] <266920839+paseo-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1791112300 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791112300 +0200\n\nfix(server): keep a stuck directory search from blocking every other search (#6041)\n\nDirectory search shares two filesystem slots across all searches. Searches\nover one tree walk it in the same order, so two Add Project searches that\nreach the same folder whose read never returns held both slots, and every\nlater directory search queued behind them: command center file search,\n@-file autocomplete, and file-link lookups in unrelated folders all hung\nuntil the read returned.\n\nSearches waiting on the same path now share its pending filesystem call, so\none stuck folder holds one slot and the other stays free.\n\nRefs #4879\n\nCo-authored-by: paseo-bot[bot] <266920839+paseo-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>",
